            "body": "## zizmor / \n\nunpinned action reference: action is not pinned to a hash (required by blanket policy)\n\n[Show more details](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/security/code-scanning/87)",
            "commit_id": "a76fc6686d1723341eef0192b3e4771c930b37d6",
            "created_at": "2026-07-08T13:32:39Z",
            "diff_hunk": "@@ -0,0 +1,76 @@\n+# Composite action: cross-compile Neovim to WebAssembly.\n+#\n+# This is the heavy, shared half of the wasm pipeline — emscripten + the native\n+# host helpers + the wasm cross-compile + the runtime variant packaging (which\n+# includes the per-variant boot gate). Callers run tests against the build\n+# and/or assemble the static demo bundle from it (wasm/web/build-site.sh).\n+name: Build wasm\n+description: Cross-compile Neovim to wasm (engine + runtime data packages).\n+\n+inputs:\n+  em-version:\n+    description: Emscripten version to pin (must have -sJSPI).\n+    required: false\n+    default: \"3.1.69\"\n+\n+runs:\n+  using: composite\n+  steps:\n+    - name: Install host build deps\n+      shell: bash\n+      run: |\n+        sudo apt-get update\n+        sudo apt-get install -y ninja-build gettext cmake unzip curl build-essential\n+\n+    # Node 26 is the version wasm/README.md documents as tested for JSPI\n+    # (WebAssembly.Suspending) — REQUIRED to run the wasm engine under Node.\n+    # build-nvim.sh runs `node nvim.js` to verify each runtime variant boots clean\n+    # AND to generate the full variant's help-tag database (doc/tags). Node 20\n+    # lacks JSPI (the verify gate then passed vacuously and :help shipped\n+    # untagged); Node 24 still gates JSPI behind a flag — 26 has it on by default.\n+    - uses: actions/setup-node@v4\n+      with:\n+        node-version: 26\n+\n+    # Emscripten, pinned to the version the wasm build was developed against.\n+    - name: Setup Emscripten\n+      uses: mymindstorm/setup-emsdk@v14",
